From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ram: generate_ram -zero_word, a word that reads 0
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

-zero_word n makes word n read 0 and drop its writes, as a RISC-V
register file's x0: its row keeps its place in the grid but has no
flops and no clock gate, and the AND-OR read trees are built over the
other rows; where the storage flop's output is inverted the zero word
stays in them, its term its own select, so the inverter at the root
reads it as 0. The behavioral model reads 0 there and ignores writes.
Needs -read_style and_or and -column_mux_ratio 1 (RAM-0060).

Tested: src/ram/test/zero_word_asap7.tcl.

Commit 3 of 23 in OpenROAD #11723, carried here from it. Not
upstreamed; retires at a //:bump onto an OpenROAD that has it.
